language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Fill the n x n grid with digits 1 to n so that every row, column and 3 x 3 nonet holds each digit once, and every cage sums to its target without repeating a digit.
given n : int(1..)
given problem_1 : matrix indexed by [int(1..problem_1_dim1)] of int(0..)
given problem_2 : matrix indexed by [int(1..problem_2_dim1), int(1..problem_2_dim2), int(1..problem_2_dim3)] of int(0..)
given problem_2_len : matrix indexed by [int(1..problem_2_dim1)] of int(1..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n)

branching on [x]
heuristic sdf

such that
$ each row contains each digit exactly once
forAll r : int(1..n) . allDiff([x[r, c] | c : int(1..n)]),
$ each column contains each digit exactly once
forAll c : int(1..n) . allDiff([x[r, c] | r : int(1..n)]),
$ each 3 x 3 nonet contains each digit exactly once
forAll b : int(0..2) . forAll bb : int(0..2) . allDiff([x[3 * b + r, 3 * bb + s] | r : int(1..3), s : int(1..3)]),
$ the cells of each cage sum to the cage target
forAll c : int(1..problem_2_dim1) . (sum([x[problem_2[c, k, 1], problem_2[c, k, 2]] | k : int(1..problem_2_len[c])]) = problem_1[c]),
$ no digit is repeated within a cage
forAll c : int(1..problem_2_dim1) . allDiff([x[problem_2[c, k, 1], problem_2[c, k, 2]] | k : int(1..problem_2_len[c])])
